<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piet Retief</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1838">1838</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pieter Mauritz Retief</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piet Retief was a Voortrekker leader from the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> who led a party of emigrants into Natal during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-trek">Great Trek</a>. In February 1838, while negotiating a land grant, he and his companions were killed on the orders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mgungundlovu">uMgungundlovu</a>. Their deaths led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-blood-river">Battle of Blood River</a> later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piet-retief.jpg" alt="Piet Retief" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joonas Lyytinen, Käyttäjä:Joonasl · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voortrekker_Monument_May_2006,_IMG_3003.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
